---
title: Widgets
description: The blocks of a sidebar — who wrote this, what is popular, where you are in a series, what the author uses, a way to say thank you, a newsletter. One frame, sixteen contents; stack them in a column beside an article or a feed.
eyebrow: Component
source: src/components/widget.css
---
<p>A widget is a <strong>frame</strong> and something inside it. The frame is always the same — a ruled block, a mono caption, an optional link on the right — and everything below is what goes in. Each one here stands alone: copy the markup, drop it in a column, done.</p>

{{#example title="A column of them" surface=true}}
<aside class="im-widgets" style="max-width: 19rem" aria-label="Sidebar">
	<section class="im-widget" style="background-color: var(--im-canvas)">
		<h2 class="im-widget-title">Most read <a href="#a-column-of-them">All →</a></h2>
		<ol class="im-widget-list im-widget-list-ranked">
			{{#foreach demo.three}}<li><a href="#a-column-of-them">{{title}}<small>{{primary_tag.name}} · {{reading_time}} min</small></a></li>{{/foreach}}
		</ol>
	</section>
	<section class="im-widget im-widget-accent">
		<h2 class="im-widget-title">Newsletter</h2>
		<p class="im-widget-heading">One email when something lands.</p>
		<a class="im-btn im-btn-ink im-btn-block" href="#a-column-of-them">Subscribe {{> "icons/arrow-right"}}</a>
	</section>
</aside>
{{/example}}

<h2>The frame</h2>
<div class="im-table-scroll">
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th></th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td><code>im-widgets</code></td><td>The column. Put it in the rail of <code>im-with-aside</code> or <code>im-with-rails</code>, inside an <code>im-sticky-rail</code> if it should follow the reader.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-widget</code></td><td>One ruled block.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>… <code>im-widget-fill</code></td><td>A surface instead of a rule.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>… <code>im-widget-accent</code></td><td>The accent. For the one widget that should be seen — never two.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>… <code>im-widget-bare</code></td><td>No frame at all, for a widget used somewhere that already has one: a footer column, a card, the menu panel.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-widget-title</code></td><td>The mono caption. May hold a link on the right ("All →").</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-widget-heading</code></td><td>A larger line, for a promotional widget.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-widget-media</code></td><td>A picture that fills the top of the frame, corners and all.</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h2>Author</h2>
<p>Who wrote this. On a post page it belongs high in the column; on a collection page it belongs low or not at all — a reader scanning a list has not met anyone yet.</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 22rem"}}
<section class="im-widget im-widget-author">
	<h2 class="im-widget-title">Written by</h2>
	{{> "components/avatar" size="xl" src=demo.author.profile_image name=demo.author.name}}
	<div><a class="im-widget-author-name" href="#author">{{demo.author.name}}</a><p class="im-widget-author-role">Engineer · {{demo.author.location}}</p></div>
	<p>{{demo.author.bio}}</p>
	<div class="im-cluster"><a class="im-btn im-btn-primary im-btn-sm" href="#author">Follow</a><a class="im-btn im-btn-icon im-btn-sm" href="#author" aria-label="X">{{> "icons/brand-x"}}</a><a class="im-btn im-btn-icon im-btn-sm" href="#author" aria-label="GitHub">{{> "icons/brand-github"}}</a></div>
	<div class="im-widget-stats"><div><strong>{{demo.author.count.posts}}</strong><span>posts</span></div><div><strong>12.4k</strong><span>readers</span></div><div><strong>7</strong><span>years</span></div></div>
</section>
{{/example}}

<h2>Series</h2>
<p>Where this post sits in a run of them. It is the <a href="/components/timeline/">timeline</a> in a widget, and it is what belongs at the <strong>top of the right rail whenever there is a contents rail on the left</strong>: the contents say where you are in the post, the series says where you are in the run. The part being read is not a link to itself.</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 22rem"}}
<section class="im-widget">
	<h2 class="im-widget-title">This series <a href="#series">4 parts</a></h2>
	<ol class="im-timeline im-timeline-detailed im-widget-series">
		{{#each demo.series}}
		<li class="im-timeline-item" data-state="{{state}}">
			<span class="im-timeline-marker">{{part}}</span>
			<h3 class="im-timeline-title">{{#if url}}<a href="{{url}}">{{title}}</a>{{else}}<span>{{title}}</span>{{/if}}</h3>
		</li>
		{{/each}}
	</ol>
</section>
{{/example}}

<h2>Most read</h2>
<p>Mono numerals from a CSS counter — nothing is numbered in the markup, so the list can be reordered or cut without renumbering.</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 22rem"}}
<section class="im-widget">
	<h2 class="im-widget-title">Most read <a href="#most-read">All →</a></h2>
	<ol class="im-widget-list im-widget-list-ranked">
		{{#foreach demo.four}}<li><a href="#most-read">{{title}}<small>{{primary_tag.name}} · {{reading_time}} min</small></a></li>{{/foreach}}
	</ol>
</section>
{{/example}}

<h2>Latest</h2>
<p>The same list with a thumbnail. Use one or the other in a column, not both.</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 22rem"}}
<section class="im-widget">
	<h2 class="im-widget-title">Latest</h2>
	<ul class="im-widget-list im-widget-list-thumbs">
		{{#foreach demo.three}}<li><a href="#latest"><img src="{{feature_image}}" alt="" loading="lazy">{{title}}<small>{{date format="D MMM"}}</small></a></li>{{/foreach}}
	</ul>
</section>
{{/example}}

<h2>Things I use</h2>
<p>The tools, the camera, the chair. A name, what it is for, and where to get it — the mark on the left is a logo if there is one and the initial if there is not, so a row never collapses. Add <code>rel="sponsored"</code> to any link that pays.</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 22rem"}}
<section class="im-widget">
	<h2 class="im-widget-title">Things I use <a href="#things-i-use">All →</a></h2>
	<div class="im-widget-products">
		{{#each demo.products}}
		<a class="im-widget-product" href="#things-i-use">
			<span class="im-widget-product-mark">{{name.[0]}}</span>
			<span class="im-widget-product-name">{{name}}</span>
			<span class="im-widget-product-note">{{note}}</span>
			{{icon "arrow-up-right"}}
		</a>
		{{/each}}
	</div>
</section>
{{/example}}

<h2>Support</h2>
<p>The small version of the panel that goes under a post. The amounts are ordinary buttons: whatever a theme wires them to — a payment link, a Ghost tier, a form — is the theme's business.</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 22rem"}}
<section class="im-widget im-widget-fill">
	<h2 class="im-widget-title">Support</h2>
	<p class="im-widget-heading">Buy me a coffee</p>
	<p>Everything here is free and paid for by nobody. If it saved you an afternoon, you can send something back.</p>
	<div class="im-widget-support-amounts">
		<button class="im-btn im-btn-sm" type="button">€3</button>
		<button class="im-btn im-btn-sm" type="button">€5</button>
		<button class="im-btn im-btn-sm" type="button">€10</button>
	</div>
	<a class="im-btn im-btn-primary im-btn-block im-btn-sm" href="#support">{{> "icons/wallet"}}Send it</a>
</section>
{{/example}}

<h2>Newsletter</h2>
<p>One per page. Either the accent block with a button, or the form itself — the form if this is the only place on the page a reader can subscribe.</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 22rem"}}
<div class="im-widgets">
	<section class="im-widget im-widget-accent">
		<h2 class="im-widget-title">Newsletter</h2>
		<p class="im-widget-heading">One email when something lands.</p>
		<p>Nothing else, ever. Unsubscribe in one click.</p>
		<a class="im-btn im-btn-ink im-btn-block" href="#newsletter">Subscribe {{> "icons/arrow-right"}}</a>
	</section>
	<section class="im-widget im-widget-fill">
		<h2 class="im-widget-title">Newsletter</h2>
		<p class="im-widget-heading">Join 4,100 readers.</p>
		{{> "components/subscribe" id="widget-email" button="Join"}}
	</section>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Topics</h2>
<p>A cluster of <a href="/components/badge/#tag">tags</a> with their counts. It wraps; it does not scroll — a sidebar is not a filter bar.</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 22rem"}}
<section class="im-widget">
	<h2 class="im-widget-title">Topics</h2>
	<div class="im-cluster" style="--im-cluster-gap: .375rem">{{#foreach fixtures.tags}}<a class="im-tag" href="#topics">{{name}} <small class="text-muted">{{count.posts}}</small></a>{{/foreach}}</div>
</section>
{{/example}}

<h2>On this page</h2>
<p>The <a href="/navigation/toc/">table of contents</a>, with <code>data-toc-title=""</code> because the widget already has a caption. Use this <em>instead</em> of a contents rail, not as well as one.</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 22rem"}}
<section class="im-widget">
	<h2 class="im-widget-title">On this page</h2>
	<nav class="im-toc" data-toc="#main" data-toc-title="" aria-label="On this page (widget)"></nav>
</section>
{{/example}}

<h2>About this post</h2>
<p>A definition list: the term on the left, the value right-aligned. Facts a reader might want and the page never says out loud.</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 22rem"}}
<section class="im-widget">
	<h2 class="im-widget-title">About this post</h2>
	<dl class="im-widget-facts"><dt>Published</dt><dd>17 Sep 2026</dd><dt>Reading time</dt><dd>8 min</dd><dt>Topic</dt><dd>Travel</dd><dt>Access</dt><dd><span class="im-badge im-badge-success">Public</span></dd></dl>
</section>
{{/example}}

<h2>Now</h2>
<p>What the author is doing at the moment — reading, building, listening to. Short lines, an icon each. It dates fast, which is the point.</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 22rem"}}
<section class="im-widget">
	<h2 class="im-widget-title">Now <a href="#now">Sep 2026</a></h2>
	<ul class="im-widget-now">
		<li>{{icon "book-open"}}<span>Reading <b>The Peregrine</b>, slowly</span></li>
		<li>{{icon "code"}}<span>Building <b>this design system</b></span></li>
		<li>{{icon "map-pin"}}<span>In <b>Budapest</b> until spring</span></li>
		<li>{{icon "volume-2"}}<span>On repeat: <b>Talk Talk</b></span></li>
	</ul>
</section>
{{/example}}

<h2>Quote</h2>
<p>One line lifted out of the post, or from someone else. It is the only widget allowed to be loud, because it is the only one that is not a list.</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 22rem"}}
<section class="im-widget">
	<h2 class="im-widget-title">From the piece</h2>
	<blockquote class="im-widget-quote">Nobody on this road wants to arrive.<span class="im-widget-quote-by">Amalfi, in November</span></blockquote>
</section>
{{/example}}

<h2>Archive</h2>
<p>A year, how much of it there is, and a bar showing that as a share of the busiest year — set inline as <code>--im-share</code>. Cheap, and the only widget that shows a site has history.</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 22rem"}}
<section class="im-widget">
	<h2 class="im-widget-title">Archive</h2>
	<nav class="im-widget-archive" aria-label="Archive">
		{{#each demo.archive}}<a href="#archive" style="--im-share: {{share}}">{{year}}<small>{{posts}}</small></a>{{/each}}
	</nav>
</section>
{{/example}}

<h2>Featured</h2>
<p>One post, given a picture. <code>im-widget-media</code> fills the top of the frame; the rest is an ordinary heading and line.</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 22rem"}}
{{#with demo.three.[1]}}
<section class="im-widget">
	<h2 class="im-widget-title">Editor's pick</h2>
	<span class="im-widget-media"><img src="{{feature_image}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></span>
	<p class="im-widget-heading">{{title}}</p>
	<p>{{excerpt words="18"}}</p>
	<a class="im-btn im-btn-sm" href="#featured">Read it {{> "icons/arrow-right"}}</a>
</section>
{{/with}}
{{/example}}

<h2>Sponsor</h2>
<p>Say what it is. A block that looks like editorial and is not is the fastest way to lose a reader for good.</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 22rem"}}
<section class="im-widget im-widget-sponsor">
	<h2 class="im-widget-title">Sponsor</h2>
	<span class="im-widget-media" style="--im-widget-media: 2 / 1"><img src="{{demo.six.[4].feature_image}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></span>
	<p class="im-widget-heading">Field Notes Weekly</p>
	<p>A letter about maps, roads and the people who draw them.</p>
	<a class="im-btn im-btn-sm im-btn-block" href="#sponsor" rel="sponsored noopener">Take a look</a>
	<p class="im-widget-sponsor-label">Paid placement</p>
</section>
{{/example}}

<h2>Follow &amp; search</h2>
<p>Neither needs anything of its own: the first is a cluster of <a href="/components/share/">brand buttons</a>, the second an <a href="/forms/inputs/">input group</a>.</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 22rem"}}
<div class="im-widgets">
	<section class="im-widget">
		<h2 class="im-widget-title">Elsewhere</h2>
		<div class="im-cluster" style="--im-cluster-gap: .375rem">
			<a class="im-btn im-btn-brand im-btn-brand-soft im-btn-sm" data-brand="x" href="#follow-search">{{> "icons/brand-x"}}<span>X</span></a>
			<a class="im-btn im-btn-brand im-btn-brand-soft im-btn-sm" data-brand="github" href="#follow-search">{{> "icons/brand-github"}}<span>GitHub</span></a>
			<a class="im-btn im-btn-brand im-btn-brand-soft im-btn-sm" data-brand="youtube" href="#follow-search">{{> "icons/brand-youtube"}}<span>YouTube</span></a>
		</div>
	</section>
	<section class="im-widget">
		<h2 class="im-widget-title">Search</h2>
		<div class="im-input-group">{{icon "search"}}<input class="im-input" type="search" placeholder="Search the journal…" aria-label="Search the journal"></div>
	</section>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>In a Ghost theme</h2>
{{{{code "hbs"}}}}
<aside class="im-widgets">
	{{#primary_author}}
	<section class="im-widget im-widget-author">
		<h2 class="im-widget-title">{{t "Written by"}}</h2>
		{{> "components/avatar" size="xl" src=profile_image name=name}}
		<a class="im-widget-author-name" href="{{url}}">{{name}}</a>
		{{#if bio}}<p>{{bio}}</p>{{/if}}
	</section>
	{{/primary_author}}

	{{#get "posts" filter="featured:true" limit="5" as |popular|}}
	<section class="im-widget">
		<h2 class="im-widget-title">{{t "Most read"}}</h2>
		<ol class="im-widget-list im-widget-list-ranked">
			{{#foreach popular}}<li><a href="{{url}}">{{title}}<small>{{reading_time}}</small></a></li>{{/foreach}}
		</ol>
	</section>
	{{/get}}
</aside>
{{{{/code}}}}

<h2>Choosing</h2>
<ul>
	<li><strong>Three widgets is a sidebar; seven is a second page nobody reads.</strong> On a phone the column drops under the article — put the one that matters first.</li>
	<li><strong>The order says what the page is for.</strong> Post page: series, author, popular, newsletter. Collection page: newsletter, topics, archive.</li>
	<li><strong>One accent block per page.</strong> Two is none.</li>
	<li><strong>Every widget has a caption</strong>, even when it looks obvious — it is what a screen reader lands on, and <code>aria-labelledby</code> should point at it.</li>
	<li><strong>Nothing in a widget should be the only way to reach something.</strong> A sidebar is not printed on a phone until after the article, and a reader on a phone may never arrive.</li>
</ul>
